<title>INDIA: Indian exports rose 2.53 percent in June.</title>
<headline>Indian exports rose 2.53 percent in June.</headline>
<dateline>NEW DELHI 1997-08-01</dateline>
<text>
<p>Indian merchandise exports increased to  $2.66 billion in June, up 2.53 percent from $2.59 billion in the same  month in 1996, the government said on Friday.  </p>
<p>    MERCHANDISE TRADE   Jun 97    May 97     Jun 96</p>
<p>    Exports		  2.66	2.86	 2.59</p>
<p>    Imports		  3.11	3.21	 2.81</p>
<p>    Trade balance	 -0.45     -0.35	-0.22</p>
<p>Note - Figures, in billions of dollars, may not add up due to rounding.   </p>
<p>Indian merchandise exports dipped 0.95 percent in April-June 1997  to $8.13 billion from $8.21 in the same period a year ago, the statement  said.</p>
<p>    MERCHANDISE TRADE   Apr-Jun 97    Apr-Jun 96</p>
<p>    Exports		    8.13	     8.21</p>
<p>    Imports		    9.53	     9.15</p>
<p>    Trade balance	   -1.39	    -0.93</p>
<p>Note - Figures are in billions of dollars and may not add up due to  rounding.</p>
<p>--New Delhi newsroom +91-11 301 2024</p>
</text>
